            <div xml:id="d222">

                <pb facs="0382" n="294" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg294"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/2967: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Feely</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-03-23T11:00:00-04:00">March 23, 1933—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>23. There is every indication that the Bolivian Government will not accept a
                    suspension of hostilities, even on the basis of positions actually held, unless
                    and until a prior agreement has been made for the settlement of the fundamental
                    question.</p>
                <pb facs="0383" n="295" xml:id="pg295"/>
                <p>Recent military successes and the acquiescence of Chile in the free transit of
                    arms via Arica have greatly strengthened Bolivian confidence in a successful
                    issue of the military campaign.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Feely</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
